    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1874 Philander Hulett built a boat landing, general store, and post office, sparking the hamlet’s development.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huletts_Landing%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The hamlet’s only roadway access is County Route 6, running north–south along the eastern shore of Lake George.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huletts_Landing%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Huletts Landing sits entirely within Adirondack Park, on Lake George’s northeastern shore.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
